From b83036b117a1428fa150089222ef694c54f79ae8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 13:35:57 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add icon shapes and numbered badges 1-12 for /tag

Tags can show a colored arrow, the stop sign or the paw today. Raid
marking wants more distinct symbols: the familiar skull / X / sword /
diamond / flame / star set, and numbers for kill or crowd-control order,
so a caller can say "kill skull, then 3" and everyone sees it.

- Icon keys after '^': K skull, X red X, A gold sword, D blue diamond,
  F green flame, T purple star, L wolf's head (the one free letter in
  "wolf"). They avoid R/O/Y/G/B/W/P/S on purpose: an
  older client reads only the first key character, so a free letter shows
  the text with no shape rather than a different, wrong one.
- Numbered badges ^1^ to ^12^: a white disc with block digits. "^10^" to
  "^12^" are read as two-digit keys (only when both characters are digits
  and a '^' follows, so no existing prefix changes meaning). The digits sit
  on each face separately, the back copy mirrored, so a badge reads
  correctly from either side.
- tag_shapes.cpp/.h (new): the geometry, with no DirectX dependency. Every
  shape is flat parts extruded to the same thickness as the octagon and
  paw; each part is convex (or star-shaped about its center) so it
  triangulates as a simple fan. Concave outlines come from overlapping
  parts, and detail (eye sockets, teeth, the sword's fuller, the diamond's
  facet, digits) is a part standing slightly proud of the face in a dark,
  light or contrasting accent tone. No textures, no concave triangulation.
- TagArrows builds the meshes at startup, colors them with the existing
  face gradients plus the accent tones, and sizes the vertex buffer to
  hold every shape at once alongside the arrow color cache.
- The shape is now picked from the tag's own color rather than after a
  nameplate color is substituted, so a nameplate color can no longer
  collide with a shape's color.
- Prettyprint, the target tooltip and /tag help name the new shapes.
- README: the new keys and examples.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
